From 503bb3941a945eef93b7a93e2fb14c06a77545b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:33:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Behaviours: functions of batches and of a point detected
 independently

As for the material properties, the functions of batches of points exist if
and only if the library exports `<name>_generic_parallel_api_version`
(`BehaviourDescription::batch_api_version`, read by
`isGenericParallelBehaviour`), and the functions of a point if and only if
the library exports `Generic` as interface (or no interface). Both are loaded
when a library of the `generic-parallel` interface also contains the
functions of the `generic` interface; `checkBatchInterface` applies this
rule for both kinds of functions.
---
